abstract: The Hakai Institute Seagrass Bioblitz (2018) was an intensive biodiversity
  survey of the seagrass beds around Calvert Island, BC. Whenever possible, teams
  of taxonomists and field biologists made collections of specimens that were morphologically
  identified in the lab, photographed, and then processed for DNA barcoding, with
  the resulting sequence data added to the Barcode of Life Datasystem (BOLD). This
  survey provided a wealth of detailed information about the diversity of marine invertebrates
  and fish inhabiting seagrass beds around Calvert Island.
